1
00:00:01,585 --> 00:00:02,920
HEY!

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,254
HEY.

3
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:05,840
LISTEN, YOU GUYS THINK

4
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,758
I HAVE A CHANCE
WITH JANINE?

5
00:00:07,758 --> 00:00:09,885
OH, HONEY, WE HAVE
BEEN THROUGH THIS BEFORE.

6
00:00:09,885 --> 00:00:11,512
YEAH. DON'T DO
THIS TO YOURSELF.

7
00:00:11,512 --> 00:00:13,931
SHE MADE IT PRETTY CLEAR
IT IS NOT GOING TO HAPPEN.

8
00:00:13,931 --> 00:00:15,557
WELL, ALL RIGHT, THEN.

9
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:18,101
I GUESS I SHOULDN'T
GET TOO EXCITED ABOUT THE FACT

10
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:19,478
THAT I JUST KISSED HER!

11
00:00:19,478 --> 00:00:21,188
ARE YOU SERIOUS?!

12
00:00:21,188 --> 00:00:22,272
REALLY?

13
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:23,816
YEAH? WELL, WE'LL SEE.

14
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:27,068
YOU KISSED HER?

15
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:29,279
OH, WE KISSED IT UP REAL NICE.

16
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:30,781
SO YOU
KISSED HER.

17
00:00:30,781 --> 00:00:32,950
SO WHAT HAPPENED AFTER THAT?

18
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:36,453
I CAME OVER HERE
TO TELL YOU GUYS.

19
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:38,789
SO SHE'S JUST WAITING
OVER THERE FOR YOU?

20
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:41,709
YEAH.

21
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:56,515
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

22
00:00:56,515 --> 00:00:58,809
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

23
00:00:58,809 --> 00:01:01,020
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

24
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:04,982
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

25
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:08,276
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

26
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:10,487
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

27
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:14,825
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

28
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:20,330
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

29
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:28,839
I GOT TO GO.

30
00:01:28,839 --> 00:01:30,089
OKAY.

31
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:34,887
I'M GOING TO BE
REALLY LATE FOR DANCE CLASS.

32
00:01:34,887 --> 00:01:36,179
OKAY.

33
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,059
OKAY, NOW
I'M REALLY LEAVING.

34
00:01:40,059 --> 00:01:41,643
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.
OKAY.

35
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:44,103
BUT, HEY, CAN YOU JUST...
JUST LEAVE YOUR LIPS?

36
00:01:46,941 --> 00:01:47,942
BYE.

37
00:01:47,942 --> 00:01:48,901
BYE.

38
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:52,905
HAVE YOU KISSED HER YET?

39
00:01:54,782 --> 00:01:56,075
IT'S AWESOME.

40
00:01:56,075 --> 00:01:58,326
YOU KNOW, I COULD DO IT FOREVER.

41
00:01:58,326 --> 00:01:59,661
YOU KNOW WHAT?

42
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:02,998
SHE KISSES BETTER
THAN MY MOM COOKS.

43
00:02:02,998 --> 00:02:06,710
I AM SO GLAD YOU
SAID "COOKS."

44
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,754
OH, HEY, RACHEL, SWEETHEART

45
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:11,465
YOU HAVE GOT TO TELL
THE POST OFFICE THAT
YOU HAVE MOVED, OKAY?

46
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,801
WE'RE STILL GETTING
ALL YOUR BILLS AND STUFF.

47
00:02:13,801 --> 00:02:14,802
OH.

48
00:02:14,802 --> 00:02:16,011
OOH, OOH, POTTERY BARN.

49
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:17,554
YOU CAN THROW
THE REST AWAY.

50
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:19,681
I'M NOT YOUR GARBAGE MAN.

51
00:02:20,808 --> 00:02:23,018
I'M YOUR MAILMAN.

52
00:02:23,018 --> 00:02:24,478
MONICA, LOOK.

53
00:02:24,478 --> 00:02:25,646
LOOK, LOOK, LOOK.

54
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:27,397
HERE IS THAT TABLE
THAT I ORDERED.

55
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:28,607
AH...

56
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:30,317
YOU GOT IT FROM
POTTERY BARN?

57
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:31,568
YEAH.

58
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:32,987
IT'S AN APOTHECARY
TABLE.

59
00:02:32,987 --> 00:02:35,614
DOES ANYONE EVEN KNOW
WHAT AN APOTHECARY IS?

60
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:37,032
A PHARMACIST.

61
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:39,618
( imitating mockingly ):
"A PHARMACIST."

62
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:44,414
RACH, PHOEBE HATES
POTTERY BARN.

63
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:46,166
I HATE POTTERY BARN, TOO.

64
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:49,461
THEY KICKED ME OUT OF THERE
JUST BECAUSE I SAT ON A BED.

65
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:52,297
YOU TOOK OFF YOUR PANTS
AND CLIMBED UNDER THE SHEETS.

66
00:02:54,341 --> 00:02:56,301
I WAS TIRED.

67
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:00,097
PHOEBE HATES
POTTERY BARN?

68
00:03:00,097 --> 00:03:02,390
YEAH, SHE HATES ALL
MASS-PRODUCED STUFF.

69
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:06,103
SHE THINKS HER FURNITURE
SHOULD HAVE A HISTORY--
A STORY BEHIND IT.

70
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:08,522
THIS HAS
A STORY BEHIND IT.

71
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:09,940
THEY HAD TO SHIP IT

72
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:13,777
ALL THE WAY FROM
THE WHITE PLAINS STORE.

73
00:03:13,777 --> 00:03:15,863
IT'S GOT TO BE
ONE OF A KIND.

74
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:17,364
YOU KNOW, LIKE
THE, UM....

75
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:20,241
WHAT'S THAT GOD-AWFUL
CERAMIC FRUIT BOWL

76
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:21,660
THAT SHE HAS ON
HER COUNTER?

77
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:24,579
HEY, I MADE THAT FOR HER.

78
00:03:25,789 --> 00:03:27,124
YOU MADE POTTERY?

79
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:29,417
YEAH. I MADE IT
OUT OF THIS FRUIT BOWL

80
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:30,919
I FOUND IN THE GARBAGE.

81
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:32,295
I'M TELLING YOU

82
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,798
IF YOU PUT THAT
IN HER APARTMENT

83
00:03:34,798 --> 00:03:36,800
YOU WILL NEVER
HEAR THE END OF IT.

84
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,510
OKAY, FINE, I'LL
JUST TELL HER

85
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:40,721
THAT IT'S AN ANTIQUE
APOTHECARY TABLE.

86
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:43,264
SHE DOESN'T HAVE TO KNOW
WHERE IT CAME FROM.

87
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:44,933
OH, I LOVE
THESE LITTLE DRAWERS.

88
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:47,477
OH, LOOK, LOOK, IT SAYS
THAT IT HOLDS 300 CDs.

89
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:50,605
AH, JUST LIKE
THE APOTHECARY TABLES OF YORE.

90
00:03:58,197 --> 00:03:59,990
SO THEN THE
FARMER SAYS

91
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:03,243
"THAT'S NOT A COW AND
YOU'RE NOT MILKING."

92
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:05,244
I AM SO GLAD
THAT YOU GUYS GOT TOGETHER.

93
00:04:05,244 --> 00:04:06,914
CHANDLER AND I
ARE ALWAYS LOOKING

94
00:04:06,914 --> 00:04:09,457
FOR A COUPLE TO GO OUT WITH,
AND NOW WE HAVE ONE.

95
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:11,585
LOOK AT US-- WE'RE
A COUPLE OF COUPLES.

96
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:13,587
I HAD SO MUCH
FUN TONIGHT.

97
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:15,338
AND WHAT A
GREAT RESTAURANT.

98
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:16,840
YEAH, YEAH, AND CHANDLER

99
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:19,885
I CAN'T BELIEVE I LET YOU
PAY FOR THIS ONE.

100
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,764
THANKS AGAIN, MAN.

101
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:25,682
SO IF YOU GUYS WANT
TO COME OVER TOMORROW

102
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:28,102
I'LL MAKE THAT PASTA THING
I WAS TELLING YOU ABOUT.

103
00:04:28,102 --> 00:04:29,186
OH, THAT WOULD
BE GREAT.

104
00:04:29,186 --> 00:04:30,270
BUT, HEY, LOOK

105
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,355
AT LEAST LET US
BRING THE WINE.

106
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:33,899
JOEY, YOU DON'T HAVE TO.

107
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,192
I INSIST.

108
00:04:38,195 --> 00:04:39,613
YOU'LL GET
THE WINE, RIGHT?

109
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:40,614
YEAH, OKAY.

110
00:04:42,157 --> 00:04:44,325
OKAY, GOOD
NIGHT, GUYS.

111
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:45,326
SEE YOU
TOMORROW.

112
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:46,661
CAN'T WAIT.

113
00:04:50,874 --> 00:04:54,544
HOW ARE WE GOING
TO GET OUT OF THAT ONE?

114
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:59,007
WHAT?

115
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:01,843
I CAN'T HANDLE
TWO NIGHTS IN A ROW WITH THEM.

116
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:05,222
WHAT'S WRONG WITH
MONICA AND CHANDLER?

117
00:05:05,222 --> 00:05:08,683
I DON'T KNOW,
THEY'RE JUST A LITTLE... BLAH.

118
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:11,311
"BLAH"?

119
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:14,064
WELL, YOU KNOW, HE'S BLAH.

120
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:15,565
SHE'S JUST...

121
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:18,485
SHE'S VERY LOUD
FOR SUCH A SMALL PERSON.

122
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:23,323
UH, THEY'RE, LIKE,
MY BEST FRIENDS.

123
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:25,826
ARE YOU SAYING WE CAN'T
HANG OUT WITH THEM

124
00:05:25,826 --> 00:05:28,120
'CAUSE THAT WOULD BE
KIND OF A PROBLEM.

125
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:30,831
OF COURSE WE CAN STILL
HANG OUT WITH THEM.

126
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:33,208
JUST, YOU KNOW, NOT TWO
NIGHTS IN A ROW.

127
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,211
OKAY?

128
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:38,255
I GUESS.

129
00:05:38,255 --> 00:05:39,464
THANK YOU.

130
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:42,341
HMM.

131
00:05:42,341 --> 00:05:44,261
IF YOU WANT,
I'LL SELL MY FRIENDS

132
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:46,596
AND USE THE MONEY
TO BUY YOU PRESENTS.

133
00:05:51,977 --> 00:05:53,394
HEY.

134
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:54,771
HEY.

135
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:57,482
OOH, WHAT A GREAT TABLE.

136
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:59,734
WHERE? WHERE DID YOU GET IT?

137
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:01,111
GUESS.

138
00:06:01,111 --> 00:06:03,071
UM, A FLEA MARKET.

139
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,823
OH!

140
00:06:04,823 --> 00:06:07,659
SEE, I KNEW. I KNEW YOU WOULD
GET IT ON THE FIRST GUESS.

141
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:09,452
ISN'T IT COOL?

142
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:11,205
IT'S AN APOTHECARY
TABLE.

143
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:13,290
WOW...

144
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:16,584
OH, YOU CAN JUST IMAGINE THAT
THIS IS WHERE THEY KEPT ALL

145
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:19,671
THE STUFF TO MAKE
THEIR POTIONS, YOU KNOW.

146
00:06:19,671 --> 00:06:20,881
YES.

147
00:06:20,881 --> 00:06:22,883
YOU CAN ALMOST
SMELL THE OPIUM.

148
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:26,928
ALMOST.

149
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,222
OH, HOW MUCH WAS IT?

150
00:06:28,222 --> 00:06:30,307
ONLY 500 BUCKS.

151
00:06:30,307 --> 00:06:32,142
500 BUCKS AT A FLEA MARKET?

152
00:06:32,142 --> 00:06:34,477
OH, OKAY, SEE,
I THOUGHT YOU MEANT

153
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:36,646
HOW MUCH WAS IT
WHEN IT WAS NEW

154
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,106
YOU KNOW,
LIKE BACK THEN?

155
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:39,482
OH, NO.

156
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:41,360
I MEAN, IT WAS
AT A FLEA MARKET

157
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,196
SO IT WAS, YOU KNOW,
IT WAS, LIKE, A DOLLAR.

158
00:06:44,196 --> 00:06:45,822
A DOLLAR?

159
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,406
AND 50.

160
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:50,327
SO, YOU KNOW, IT WAS,
LIKE, ONE AND 50 DOLLARS.

161
00:06:50,327 --> 00:06:52,662
OH, OKAY, THEY GAVE YOU
THE OLD-TIME PRICING.

162
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:54,331
YEAH.

163
00:06:54,331 --> 00:06:57,209
WELL, WHAT PERIOD
IS IT FROM?

164
00:06:57,209 --> 00:06:58,626
UH, IT'S FROM YORE.

165
00:06:58,626 --> 00:07:01,296
LIKE THE DAYS OF YORE, YOU KNOW.

166
00:07:01,296 --> 00:07:03,548
YES, YES, I DO.

167
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:06,425
GOD... OH, IT'S
JUST PERFECT.

168
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:09,596
WOW, I BET IT HAS
A GREAT STORY
BEHIND IT, TOO.

169
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:12,266
DID THEY TELL YOU ANYTHING?
LIKE, YOU KNOW,
WHERE IT'S FROM OR...?

170
00:07:12,266 --> 00:07:14,851
OH, YES, THAT I KNOW.
THIS IS FROM, UH,
WHITE PLAINS.

171
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:16,061
( gasps )

172
00:07:16,061 --> 00:07:17,896
WHITE PLAINS.

173
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:19,314
MM-HMM.

174
00:07:19,314 --> 00:07:21,358
OH, IT SOUNDS LIKE
SUCH A MAGICAL PLACE.

175
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:27,114
HEY! I'M HERE.

176
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:28,282
HEY.

177
00:07:28,282 --> 00:07:31,118
OH... OH, MY GOD.

178
00:07:31,118 --> 00:07:32,202
YOU LIKE IT?

179
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:33,412
OH, MY GOD.

180
00:07:33,412 --> 00:07:36,206
IT'S MY NEW
APOTHECARY TABLE.

181
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:38,457
ROSS, PHOEBE IS GOING
TO BE HERE ANY SECOND.

182
00:07:38,457 --> 00:07:39,667
SHE CANNOT SEE THIS.

183
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:41,753
WELL, WHY NOT?
SHE'LL LOVE IT.

184
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:42,963
IT'S THE REAL THING.

185
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:44,547
I GOT IT AT POTTERY BARN.

186
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:46,465
I KNOW YOU DID.
I BOUGHT THE SAME ONE.

187
00:07:46,465 --> 00:07:48,927
AND IF SHE SEES YOUR TABLE,
SHE'S GOING TO KNOW

188
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:50,262
THAT I LIED TO HER.

189
00:07:50,262 --> 00:07:52,139
I TOLD HER THAT OURS
WAS AN ORIGINAL.

190
00:07:52,139 --> 00:07:53,390
WHY DID YOU DO THAT?

191
00:07:53,390 --> 00:07:55,558
BECAUSE SHE HATES POTTERY BARN.

192
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:59,062
SHE HATES POTTERY BARN?

193
00:07:59,062 --> 00:08:00,730
I KNOW, I KNOW.

194
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,941
SHE SAYS IT'S ALL MASS-PRODUCED;
NOTHING IS AUTHENTIC

195
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:05,360
AND EVERYONE WINDS UP
HAVING THE SAME STUFF.

196
00:08:07,528 --> 00:08:10,031
SO, COME ON. SHE'S GOING
TO BE HERE ANY SECOND.

197
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,741
CAN WE PLEASE JUST
COVER THIS UP

198
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:13,118
WITH SOMETHING, PLEASE.

199
00:08:13,118 --> 00:08:15,454
NO, NO. I AM NOT
GOING TO HIDE IT FROM PHOEBE.

200
00:08:15,454 --> 00:08:18,415
OH, ALTHOUGH I DID GET SOME
GREAT POTTERY BARN SHEETS.

201
00:08:18,415 --> 00:08:19,624
OOH!

202
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:22,419
OH, I FORGOT THEY MADE SHEETS.

203
00:08:22,419 --> 00:08:23,878
YAH.

204
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:28,216
I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE
SHE HATES POTTERY BARN.

205
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:29,343
ROSS, GET OVER IT.

206
00:08:29,343 --> 00:08:31,052
IT'S NOT LIKE SHE HATES YOU.

207
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:33,388
YEAH, BUT POTTERY BARN.

208
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:36,933
YOU KNOW WHAT I THINK?

209
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:38,810
SHE'S WEIRD, YOU KNOW.

210
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:40,437
IT'S BECAUSE SHE'S A TWIN.

211
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:42,439
TWINS ARE WEIRD.

212
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:44,274
ROSS, SHE'S NOT WEIRD.

213
00:08:44,274 --> 00:08:47,110
SHE JUST LIKES HER STUFF
TO BE ONE OF A KIND.

214
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,946
YOU KNOW WHAT'S NOT
ONE OF A KIND?

215
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,823
A TWIN.

216
00:08:53,367 --> 00:08:54,368
HEY.

217
00:08:54,368 --> 00:08:55,369
HEY.

218
00:08:55,369 --> 00:08:56,619
OH, PHOEBE'S HERE.

219
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:57,954
SO LET'S TURN OUT
ALL THE LIGHTS

220
00:08:57,954 --> 00:08:59,456
AND WE'LL JUST
WATCH THE MOVIE.

221
00:08:59,456 --> 00:09:01,624
OKAY. HEY, OOH,
COOL SHEET.

222
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:03,251
OH, YOU LIKE IT?

223
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:05,212
YOU WANT TO KNOW
WHERE I GOT IT?

224
00:09:05,212 --> 00:09:06,213
SURE.

225
00:09:06,213 --> 00:09:07,755
HE GOT IT AT A FLEA MARKET.

226
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:10,925
YOU BOUGHT YOUR SHEETS
AT A FLEA MARKET?

227
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:13,761
ROSS, YOU'VE GOT TO LOOSEN

228
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:14,762
THE PURSE STRINGS A LITTLE.

229
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:19,559
HEY.
HEY.

230
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:20,977
DINNER WILL BE READY
IN 20 MINUTES.

231
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,270
I'M SO EXCITED.

232
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,771
HERE IS THE BOTTLE
OF WINE FOR YOU

233
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:26,816
TO BRING
OVER TONIGHT.

234
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,109
YOU WERE GOING TO BUY
MONICA FLOWERS

235
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:29,528
BUT YOU COULDN'T
AFFORD IT

236
00:09:29,528 --> 00:09:31,446
BECAUSE YOU PAID FOR
DINNER LAST NIGHT.

237
00:09:31,446 --> 00:09:33,031
THANKS, THANKS.

238
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:36,159
BUT, UH, ACTUALLY, IT'S
JUST GOING TO BE ME TONIGHT.

239
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:37,327
WHAT HAPPENED
TO JANINE?

240
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:40,372
WELL, SHE'S, UH,
REALLY SICK.

241
00:09:40,372 --> 00:09:42,123
OH, THAT'S TOO BAD.

242
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:44,125
YEAH, SHE'S BEEN
IN THERE ALL DAY.

243
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:45,793
HIGH FEVER, NOSE PROBLEM...

244
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:49,964
IT'S... PHLEGM, PHLEGM,
PHLEGM, PHLEGM, PHLEGM.

245
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:51,925
( door opening )

246
00:09:51,925 --> 00:09:54,344
MONICA, CHANDLER.

247
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:58,098
I'M REALLY, REALLY
SORRY ABOUT TONIGHT.

248
00:09:58,098 --> 00:09:59,724
I DON'T KNOW
IF JOEY TOLD YOU

249
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:02,352
BUT I JUST COULDN'T
GET OUT OF GOING
TO THIS PLAY.

250
00:10:02,352 --> 00:10:03,311
I'M SORRY.

251
00:10:05,397 --> 00:10:07,566
HAVE A GREAT TIME, HUH?

252
00:10:07,566 --> 00:10:09,025
BYE.

253
00:10:11,361 --> 00:10:12,779
THAT'S FUNNY.

254
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:14,281
I SAW NO PHLEGM.

255
00:10:19,578 --> 00:10:20,912
NO, NO,
SHE REALLY IS SICK.

256
00:10:20,912 --> 00:10:22,539
THEN WHY IS SHE
GOING TO A PLAY?

257
00:10:22,539 --> 00:10:24,082
UH, WELL, YOU KNOW--

258
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:27,752
STARVE A FEVER,
GO TO A PLAY FOR A COLD.

259
00:10:29,421 --> 00:10:32,132
JOEY, WHY IS JANINE NOT
COMING OVER FOR DINNER?

260
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:33,592
WELL, UH

261
00:10:33,592 --> 00:10:35,469
SHE DIDN'T WANT TO HANG OUT
WITH YOU GUYS

262
00:10:35,469 --> 00:10:36,511
TWO NIGHTS IN A ROW.

263
00:10:36,511 --> 00:10:38,555
I'M SO SORRY.

264
00:10:38,555 --> 00:10:41,682
WHY DOES SHE NOT WANT
TO HANG OUT WITH US?

265
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:46,980
BECAUSE SHE, UH, SHE...
SHE THINKS THAT YOU ARE BLAH

266
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:49,023
AND-AND THAT YOU

267
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:51,818
MONICA, ARE TOO LOUD.

268
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:53,320
( loudly ):
WHAT?!

269
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:56,615
( hushed ):
WHAT?

270
00:10:56,615 --> 00:10:58,032
SO SHE WAS JUST PRETENDING

271
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:59,659
TO HAVE A GOOD TIME
LAST NIGHT?

272
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,119
SHE WAS LYING
TO OUR FACES?

273
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:03,121
Monica:
I CAN'T
BELIEVE THIS.

274
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:04,747
I MEAN, WHO IS
SHE TO JUDGE US?

275
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,707
WE COULD NOT HAVE
BEEN NICER TO HER.

276
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:07,708
AND I AM NOT BLAH.

277
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:08,876
I AM A HOOT.

278
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:10,295
I KNOW, I KNOW.

279
00:11:10,295 --> 00:11:12,297
YOU GUYS,
DON'T BE MAD.

280
00:11:12,297 --> 00:11:14,633
I'M SURE SHE JUST SAID
THAT STUFF

281
00:11:14,633 --> 00:11:15,883
BECAUSE SHE WAS
NERVOUS 'CAUSE

282
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:17,385
YOU GUYS ARE,
LIKE, MY BEST FRIENDS.

283
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:20,472
YOU KNOW,
AND IT WAS OUR FIRST DATE

284
00:11:20,472 --> 00:11:23,391
PLUS, SHE'S REALLY SICK.

285
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:27,521
NO, NO, YOU SAID
YOU MADE THAT UP.

286
00:11:27,521 --> 00:11:28,855
I KNOW, BUT DON'T YOU THINK
THE SICK THING

287
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:30,649
IS WAY BETTER
THAN THE PLAY THING?

288
00:11:30,649 --> 00:11:32,150
WELL, THEY'RE BOTH GOOD.

289
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:34,944
I GENERALLY JUST GO
WITH MONICA'S DRUNK AGAIN.

290
00:11:37,155 --> 00:11:39,115
COME ON, YOU GUYS,
COME ON, PLEASE, PLEASE

291
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,659
JUST GIVE HER
ANOTHER CHANCE, HUH?

292
00:11:40,659 --> 00:11:41,909
SHE'LL COME AROUND,
I PROMISE.

293
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:43,286
OF COURSE WE WILL.

294
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:45,580
COME ON, WE'VE
GOT TO MAKE DINNER.

295
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:46,956
OKAY.

296
00:11:51,628 --> 00:11:53,171
Monica:
I DO NOT LIKE THAT WOMAN!

297
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:56,341
I CAN HEAR YOU!

298
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:58,009
Monica:
I AM LOUD.

299
00:12:01,012 --> 00:12:03,097
( together)
AW.

300
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:06,685
( all laughing )

301
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,690
HEY, PHEEBS, CAN YOU PLEASE
NOT PUT YOUR FEET UP

302
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:13,066
ON MY NEW...

303
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:15,068
OLD SHEET?

304
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,069
OH, SURE.

305
00:12:16,069 --> 00:12:17,612
OH!
AAH!

306
00:12:17,612 --> 00:12:20,031
MY APOTHECARY TABLE!

307
00:12:20,031 --> 00:12:21,366
WHAT?!

308
00:12:21,366 --> 00:12:23,284
NO!

309
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:24,911
ROSS, WHERE
DID YOU GET THIS?!

310
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:26,745
I GOT IT
AT POTTERY BARN, OKAY?!

311
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:31,251
OH, MY GOD!

312
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:33,878
PHOEBE, POTTERY BARN
HAS RIPPED OFF

313
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,880
THE DESIGN OF OUR ANTIQUE!

314
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,716
( gasping ):
WOW! OH, MY GOD!

315
00:12:37,716 --> 00:12:40,093
WELL, IF THEY'VE RIPPED
OFF OUR TABLE

316
00:12:40,093 --> 00:12:44,723
OURS MUST BE WORTH
MUCH MORE THAN ONE
AND 50 DOLLARS.

317
00:12:44,723 --> 00:12:47,475
WOW, THIS DOESN'T
EVEN SMELL LIKE OPIUM.

318
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:49,894
OF COURSE NOT,
IT SMELLS LIKE WINE

319
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:51,271
WHICH YOU SPILLED.

320
00:12:51,271 --> 00:12:53,398
AND THANKS FOR WRECKING
MY SHEET, BY THE WAY.

321
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:54,733
OH, ROSS, CALM DOWN.

322
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:57,527
I'LL GIVE YOU
THE 80 CENTS.

323
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:04,117
OKAY, ONE MORE TIME.

324
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:06,578
CHANDLER, WOULD YOU LIKE
SOME MORE ORANGE JUICE?

325
00:13:06,578 --> 00:13:07,912
PERFECT DECIBEL.

326
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:10,248
I KNOW!

327
00:13:10,248 --> 00:13:11,999
HEY.

328
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:13,543
HEY.

329
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:15,712
SO, UH, WHAT ARE YOU GUYS DOING?

330
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:16,713
OH, NOTHING.

331
00:13:16,713 --> 00:13:17,880
WE'RE JUST TALKING.

332
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,466
YOU KNOW,
BLAH, BLAH, BLAH.

333
00:13:19,466 --> 00:13:20,759
LOOK, COME ON, YOU GUYS.

334
00:13:20,759 --> 00:13:22,427
YOU SAID
YOU WERE GOING TO TRY.

335
00:13:22,427 --> 00:13:24,178
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
I CAME OVER HERE

336
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:26,514
TO INVITE YOU GUYS TO A MOVIE
WITH ME AND JANINE.

337
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:28,308
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

338
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:32,019
WELL, I'D LIKE TO,
BUT I'M...( whispering )

339
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:33,271
HA, HA, VERY FUNNY....

340
00:13:33,271 --> 00:13:34,939
LOOK, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO DO.

341
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:36,983
I REALLY WANT YOU GUYS
TO GET ALONG.

342
00:13:36,983 --> 00:13:39,277
JUST, PLEASE,
COME TO THE MOVIE WITH US.

343
00:13:39,277 --> 00:13:41,112
YOU OWE ME.
WE OWE YOU?

344
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:42,113
THAT'S RIGHT.

345
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:43,531
I HELPED YOU GUYS
OUT A LOT

346
00:13:43,531 --> 00:13:45,366
IN THE START
OF YOUR RELATIONSHIP.

347
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:47,744
I HELPED YOU SNEAK AROUND
FOR, LIKE, SIX MONTHS.

348
00:13:47,744 --> 00:13:49,454
I LOOKED LIKE AN IDIOT...

349
00:13:49,454 --> 00:13:51,247
AND-AND I WAS HUMILIATED.

350
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:53,249
AND I ONLY MADE $200.

351
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:57,671
WE DIDN'T GIVE YOU
ANY MONEY.

352
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:02,841
YOU DON'T THINK I KNOW THAT?!

353
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:08,847
I CAN'T DECIDE WHETHER
IT WOULD GO BETTER

354
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:10,558
NEXT TO THE NEW
WICKER DINING CHAIR

355
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:11,768
THE SAHARA DESK

356
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:14,187
OR THE PARKER
CONSOLE TABLE.

357
00:14:14,187 --> 00:14:15,438
WOW, I DIDN'T KNOW

358
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:16,815
THERE WAS A POTTERY BARN
UP HERE.

359
00:14:16,815 --> 00:14:19,192
I KNOW, I KNOW,
I WENT A LITTLE CRAZY.

360
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:20,652
A LITTLE?

361
00:14:20,652 --> 00:14:23,571
YOUR PLACE LOOKS LIKE PAGE 72
OF THE CATALOG.

362
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:26,324
OH, LOOK AT THAT.

363
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:31,371
THE ORNAMENTAL BIRD CAGE, LARGE.

364
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:32,372
HEY.

365
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:33,832
HEY.
HEY.

366
00:14:33,832 --> 00:14:34,833
ROSS, BE CAREFUL.

367
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:35,792
THAT IS VERY OLD.

368
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:38,795
OKAY, EARLY COLONIAL
BIRD MERCHANTS

369
00:14:38,795 --> 00:14:41,005
USED TO BRING THEIR BIRDS
TO MARKET IN THAT.

370
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,550
FASCINATING.

371
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:45,677
( Phoebe gasping )

372
00:14:45,677 --> 00:14:48,513
ANOTHER AMAZING FIND.

373
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:49,889
WOW!

374
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,433
OH, I BET THIS HAS
A GREAT STORY, TOO.

375
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:53,976
IT DOES, IT DOES.

376
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:56,979
IT IS A ROOM-SEPARATING
APPARATUS FROM COLONIAL TIME.

377
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:58,481
AH.

378
00:14:58,481 --> 00:15:00,567
HUH, A LOT OF
THIS STUFF

379
00:15:00,567 --> 00:15:02,318
IS FROM THE
COLONIAL TIMES.

380
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:05,739
HEY, WHAT ARE SOME OTHER
TIME PERIODS, RACHEL?

381
00:15:08,074 --> 00:15:09,784
WELL, THERE'S YORE...

382
00:15:11,411 --> 00:15:14,288
( clears throat ):
AND, UH...

383
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:16,499
YOU KNOW, YESTERYEAR.

384
00:15:16,499 --> 00:15:18,042
YEAH... NO, I'M TELLING YOU

385
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:20,378
RACHEL HAS SUCH A GOOD EYE
FOR THIS STUFF.

386
00:15:20,378 --> 00:15:22,255
ROSS, YOU KNOW,
IF YOU EVER DECIDE

387
00:15:22,255 --> 00:15:24,841
TO REDECORATE--
AND I THINK THAT YOU SHOULD--

388
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:28,010
YOU SHOULD ASK RACHEL TO HELP.

389
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,430
OH, HONEY,
HE DOESN'T NEED MY HELP.

390
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,599
COME ON. I THINK HE'S READY
TO GET RID OF THE...

391
00:15:32,599 --> 00:15:34,058
WHAT DID YOU CALL IT?

392
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:35,643
THE "CHEAP KNOCKOFFS"
AND "DINOSAUR JUNK."

393
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,315
REALLY?

394
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:43,192
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

395
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:45,570
SINCE YOU HAVE
SUCH A GREAT SENSE

396
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:48,656
OF WHAT I NEED,
UH, OH, HERE'S 60 BUCKS.

397
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,617
WHY DON'T YOU
TAKE PHOEBE

398
00:15:50,617 --> 00:15:53,745
DOWN TO THAT COLONIAL
FLEA MARKET OF YOURS

399
00:15:53,745 --> 00:15:55,413
AND GET ME SOME STUFF.

400
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,084
YOU KNOW WHAT?

401
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,629
I DON'T REALLY THINK
PHOEBE WANTS TO COME...

402
00:16:02,629 --> 00:16:04,631
NO, I DO WANT TO.
OH, SHE DOES WANT TO.

403
00:16:04,631 --> 00:16:06,257
SHE DOES WANT TO.

404
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:14,474
PHEEBS, I DON'T
KNOW WHAT TO SAY.

405
00:16:14,474 --> 00:16:16,434
I GUESS THE
FLEA MARKET

406
00:16:16,434 --> 00:16:17,977
WAS JUST
BETTER LAST TIME.

407
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:20,313
AT LEAST I GOT
THESE SHEETS FOR ROSS.

408
00:16:20,313 --> 00:16:21,648
YEAH.

409
00:16:21,648 --> 00:16:24,484
UGH. LOOK AT THIS,
POTTERY BARN.

410
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:26,736
YEAH, YOU KNOW WHAT?
DON'T LOOK AT IT.

411
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:28,780
SERIOUSLY,
DON'T LOOK AT IT.

412
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,573
LOOK, LOOK!
THERE'S THE COFFEE TABLE

413
00:16:30,573 --> 00:16:31,699
THEY STOLE FROM US.

414
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:34,410
AAH, THOSE BASTARDS!
LET'S GO.

415
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:37,705
HEY, THAT FAN
KIND OF LOOKS LIKE OURS

416
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,082
AND THE BIRD CAGE AND...

417
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:43,878
WAIT A SEC, THIS IS
OUR EXACT LIVING ROOM.

418
00:16:43,878 --> 00:16:46,046
NO, NO, NO, IT'S NOT.
NO, IT'S NOT.

419
00:16:46,046 --> 00:16:48,800
COME ON, PHOEBE,
OURS IS TOTALLY DIFFERENT.

420
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,092
WE DON'T HAVE THE...

421
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:51,135
WE DON'T HAVE...

422
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:52,679
WE DON'T HAVE THAT LAMP.

423
00:16:52,679 --> 00:16:55,515
AND THAT SCREEN IS,
YOU KNOW

424
00:16:55,515 --> 00:16:57,892
ON THE OTHER SIDE.

425
00:16:57,892 --> 00:17:00,937
OH, MY GOD. THIS IS WHERE
YOU GOT ALL OUR STUFF--

426
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:05,191
POTTERY BARN,
OH, MY GOD!

427
00:17:05,191 --> 00:17:07,610
OKAY, OKAY, WAIT,
I DID, ALL RIGHT,
I'M SORRY...

428
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:09,863
IT'S JUST THAT, PHOEBE,
I WANTED THIS STUFF

429
00:17:09,863 --> 00:17:12,031
AND I KNOW HOW YOU FEEL
ABOUT POTTERY BARN.

430
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:13,741
SO JUST... COME ON,
DON'T BE MAD.

431
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:15,451
BUT I AM MAD,
I AM MAD

432
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:18,872
BECAUSE THIS STUFF IS EVERYTHING
THAT IS WRONG WITH THE WORLD

433
00:17:18,872 --> 00:17:21,248
AND IT'S ALL SITTING UP
IN MY LIVING ROOM!

434
00:17:21,248 --> 00:17:22,834
AND ALL I CAN THINK
ABOUT IS

435
00:17:22,834 --> 00:17:26,128
HOW I DON'T HAVE
THAT LAMP!

436
00:17:26,128 --> 00:17:28,214
WELL, THEN, HONEY,
BUY THE LAMP.

437
00:17:28,214 --> 00:17:30,675
HEY, WE HAVE THAT
60 BUCKS FROM ROSS.

438
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:35,555
I CAN'T, I CAN'T!

439
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:37,598
UNLESS...
WELL, ARE YOU SAYING

440
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:41,185
THAT YOU WOULD MOVE OUT
IF I DIDN'T BUY THAT LAMP?

441
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:43,437
WHA...? NO! I'M NOT
GOING TO MOVE OUT.

442
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:46,232
ARE YOU SAYING
THAT YOU WOULD MOVE OUT

443
00:17:46,232 --> 00:17:48,150
IF I DIDN'T BUY
THAT LAMP?!

444
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:51,237
OH, YES! I WOULD
SO MOVE OUT.

445
00:17:51,237 --> 00:17:52,739
OKAY, THEN I DON'T
HAVE A CHOICE!

446
00:17:52,739 --> 00:17:53,907
I HAVE TO BUY THAT LAMP!

447
00:17:53,907 --> 00:17:56,409
THAT'S RIGHT.

448
00:17:56,409 --> 00:17:58,870
BUT AT LEAST
THE APOTHECARY TABLE'S REAL.

449
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:05,668
WELL, THIS WAS GREAT.

450
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:08,004
DIDN'T EVERYBODY
HAVE A GREAT TIME?

451
00:18:08,004 --> 00:18:09,422
WELL, I DID.
I REALLY DID.

452
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:10,924
YOU KNOW, GUYS,
I GOT TO SAY

453
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:12,759
I'M SORRY IF I WAS
A LITTLE WEIRD

454
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:14,552
AFTER THE LAST TIME
WE WENT OUT.

455
00:18:14,552 --> 00:18:16,596
I GUESS I WAS JUST NERVOUS
OR SOMETHING.

456
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:18,097
THAT'S TOTALLY
UNDERSTANDABLE.

457
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:19,515
YEAH, DON'T WORRY
ABOUT IT.

458
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:20,934
SO WE CAN GO OUT AGAIN?

459
00:18:20,934 --> 00:18:22,727
OH, YEAH.
ABSOLUTELY.

460
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:23,937
OH, WELL, GOOD NIGHT.

461
00:18:23,937 --> 00:18:25,229
GOOD NIGHT.
GOOD NIGHT.

462
00:18:29,859 --> 00:18:31,360
SEE, HUH?

463
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,779
WASN'T THAT FUN?

464
00:18:32,779 --> 00:18:34,906
WE HAVE GOT TO MOVE.

465
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:36,991
WHAT?

466
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:38,492
I KNEW IT!

467
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:42,747
YOU KNOW, YOU'RE NOT
SO QUIET YOURSELF, MISSY!

468
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,792
AND I'M BLAH?

469
00:18:45,792 --> 00:18:47,710
LISTEN, THE ONLY THING
THAT'S MORE BORING

470
00:18:47,710 --> 00:18:49,003
THAN WATCHING
MODERN DANCE

471
00:18:49,003 --> 00:18:51,129
IS HAVING TO LISTEN
TO YOU TALK ABOUT IT.

472
00:18:51,129 --> 00:18:54,300
( imitating Janine ):
"OH, CHANDLER, I JUST LOST
MYSELF IN THE MOVEMENT."

473
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:58,012
YOU KNOW,
I KNOW YOU'RE TALKING

474
00:18:58,012 --> 00:19:00,098
BUT ALL I HEAR IS,
"BLAH, BLAH, BLAH

475
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:01,641
BLAH, BLAH."

476
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:04,978
ALL RIGHT, YOU AND ME,
LET'S GO, RIGHT NOW!

477
00:19:04,978 --> 00:19:06,479
ALL RIGHT, ENOUGH, ENOUGH!

478
00:19:06,479 --> 00:19:08,230
ENOUGH, ENOUGH!

479
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,398
YOU TWO GO HOME.

480
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:10,691
I'VE GOT TO TALK
TO JANINE.

481
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:13,235
I REALLY THINK
YOU CAN TAKE HER.

482
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:16,114
YOU BETTER HOPE
I DON'T SEE YOU
IN THE HALLWAY!

483
00:19:16,114 --> 00:19:17,949
ALL RIGHT.

484
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:23,203
ALL RIGHT, UH...

485
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:25,498
WE'VE GOT A LITTLE BIT
OF A PROBLEM HERE.

486
00:19:25,498 --> 00:19:27,000
THESE PEOPLE ARE
MY FRIENDS.

487
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,542
YOU CAN'T TREAT
THEM THAT WAY.

488
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,544
THEY SAID STUFF TO ME, TOO,
YOU KNOW.

489
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:33,547
I KNOW, I KNOW, AND
I'M GOING TO TALK
TO THEM ABOUT IT.

490
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:35,257
BUT... THEY MEAN
SO MUCH TO ME.

491
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,301
THEY'RE LIKE MY
FAMILY, YOU KNOW.

492
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:39,720
IF YOU GUYS ARE GOING
TO BE FIGHTING

493
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,555
ALL THE TIME...

494
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:43,850
I DON'T THINK
WE CAN BE TOGETHER.

495
00:19:43,850 --> 00:19:46,393
IT JUST CAN'T
WORK, OKAY?

496
00:19:46,393 --> 00:19:47,770
IT CAN'T.

497
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:50,064
I'M VERY UPSET.

498
00:19:50,064 --> 00:19:52,525
OKAY, OKAY, WOULD IT HELP

499
00:19:52,525 --> 00:19:55,402
IF I WENT OVER
AND APOLOGIZED?

500
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:59,157
YEAH, YEAH, THAT WOULD BE
VERY HELPFUL, YEAH.

501
00:20:03,953 --> 00:20:06,914
WHAT DID I TELL YOU
ABOUT THE HALL?

502
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:11,878
I WAS JUST COMING OVER HERE
TO APOLOGIZE FOR MY BEHAVIOR.

503
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:16,132
I WOULD REALLY LIKE IT
IF WE COULD BE FRIENDS.

504
00:20:18,676 --> 00:20:23,056
WELL, I KNOW THAT
WOULD MAKE JOEY HAPPY

505
00:20:23,056 --> 00:20:26,266
SO... I WOULD
LIKE THAT, TOO.

506
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:27,267
GREAT.

507
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:28,310
COME ON.

508
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:34,400
WELL, I'M GLAD WE
WORKED THINGS OUT.
ME, TOO.

509
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,276
OKAY, I'LL SEE YOU.
BYE.

510
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:37,570
OR I'LL HEAR YOU.

511
00:20:37,570 --> 00:20:39,864
THAT'S IT, BIG GIRL,
COME ON!

512
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:44,118
WAIT!

513
00:20:46,746 --> 00:20:48,039
YOU BETTER RUN!

514
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:51,084
DID YOU HEAR THAT?

515
00:20:51,084 --> 00:20:52,251
YEAH.

516
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:54,587
WHAT AM I GOING TO DO?

517
00:20:54,587 --> 00:20:55,963
I DON'T KNOW, I'M SORRY, MAN.

518
00:20:57,757 --> 00:20:59,175
YOU WANT TO GO WATCH?

519
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:00,134
YEAH.

520
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:10,853
HEY. HOW YOU DOING?

521
00:21:10,853 --> 00:21:12,521
DID SHE MOVE OUT?

522
00:21:12,521 --> 00:21:14,481
PRETTY MUCH. YEAH.

523
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:17,026
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU BROKE UP
WITH HER JUST LIKE THAT.

524
00:21:17,026 --> 00:21:19,319
WELL, WHEN IT'S NOT RIGHT,
YOU KNOW IT.

525
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:20,404
YOU OKAY?

526
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:22,531
YEAH, I'LL BE ALL RIGHT.

527
00:21:23,783 --> 00:21:25,868
YOU KNOW WHAT
WOULD CHEER YOU UP?

528
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:27,036
WHAT?

529
00:21:27,036 --> 00:21:28,621
I'M GIVING THIS LECTURE

530
00:21:28,621 --> 00:21:31,124
ON EROSION THEORIES
TOMORROW NIGHT.

531
00:21:32,875 --> 00:21:35,169
I THINK YOU SHOULD COME.

532
00:21:37,046 --> 00:21:39,465
( laughing )

533
00:21:42,426 --> 00:21:44,344
YOU'RE RIGHT,
THAT DID CHEER ME UP.

